      "content": "Mitosis is a fundamental process where a single parent cell divides to create two genetically identical daughter cells. This crucial cell division allows for growth and tissue repair in living organisms. Understanding mitosis helps us learn how multicellular life maintains itself and replaces damaged cells effectively. It is the basic mechanism for how organisms grow and learn new structures.",
