    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To truly learn mitosis, remember it involves distinct phases: Prophase sees the chromosomes condense, followed by Metaphase, where they line up in the middle of the cell. Anaphase then separates these identical chromosomes to opposite poles, and finally, Telophase completes the division by forming two new nuclei. This process lets us understand how cells precisely duplicate their genetic information to create perfect copies for growth.",
      "source": "target",
